    <string name="changelog_version">Version %1$s</string>
    <string-array name="changelog_1_4_0">
        <item>Barcode: you can now count pieces, for example 3 biscuits instead of 25 g. Choose \"pieces\" as the unit: the grams of one piece are already filled in when the package on Open Food Facts gives them, otherwise you type them.</item>
        <item>When the serving on the package names the pieces (\"3 biscuits\", \"2 slices\"), the diary shows that name, for example \"3 biscuits (25 g)\".</item>
        <item>Recent and favorites: from + choose \"Recent\" to add a food you already used again with one tap, with the same quantity (which you can change). The heart makes it a favorite. In the manual entry too, the foods you already used show up while you type the name.</item>
        <item>A product you already scanned is found even without a connection, and the barcode remembers the grams per piece you corrected.</item>
        <item>Copy: press and hold an entry to duplicate it or copy it to another day; the icon next to a meal copies the whole meal, the one at the top the whole day.</item>
        <item>Fiber, sugars and salt: they come from Open Food Facts, the CREA tables and the AI estimate, you can type them by hand and the day total shows up in Today.</item>
        <item>Backup: in Settings → Data you export everything to a file and restore it, choosing whether to replace the data or merge it with the one on the phone. You can also export the diary as CSV for Excel.</item>
        <item>Health Connect: connect PhotoCal in Settings to see steps and burned calories in Today, write weight and water and, if you want, add the burned calories to the goal of the day.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="changelog_1_3_0">
        <item>PhotoCal checks GitHub for a new version (at startup, at most once a day, or from Settings → About) and shows you what\'s new in it before you update.</item>
        <item>The update is downloaded and installed from the app (with the permission to install apps), or in the browser.</item>
        <item>The first time you open the app after an update, it shows what\'s new; you can read it again in Settings → About.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="changelog_1_2_0">
        <item>Water: a glass counter in Today, with a goal suggested by your profile.</item>
        <item>Home screen widget with today\'s glasses and shortcuts to add a meal.</item>
        <item>Icon shortcuts: meal photo, manual meal, +1 glass and share today.</item>
        <item>Water reminders at half and at the full goal.</item>
        <item>Name and photo in the profile.</item>
        <item>Share a day or a week with a link that opens in PhotoCal.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="changelog_1_1_0">
        <item>Profile and goals: an estimate of your needs with suggested calories and macros, which you can always type by hand.</item>
        <item>Protein, carbs and fat goals, with the progress in Today.</item>
        <item>Weight log with a 30, 90 and 365 day chart.</item>
    </string-array>
